WEBVTT

00:00:00.980 --> 00:00:05.350
Akagi, Suido, and Aoi.

00:00:05.730 --> 00:00:08.610
Starting today,
I'll group all three of you together as RGB.

00:00:06.190 --> 00:00:08.940
AUGUST 5, 2011

00:00:09.230 --> 00:00:11.110
Such a nice nickname!

00:00:12.280 --> 00:00:14.610
Oh wait, I'm Suido, too.

00:00:15.320 --> 00:00:17.320
Oh well, the small details don't matter.

00:00:18.370 --> 00:00:20.200
That sounds like a hero! Awesome!

00:00:20.410 --> 00:00:23.080
I like how I'm first.

00:00:23.080 --> 00:00:26.290
Asumi, isn't it a bit crude
to group us three together?

00:00:26.460 --> 00:00:33.260
Huh? But when Shuta, Ran, and you
are together, I feel like you guys can do anything.

00:00:33.510 --> 00:00:35.130
Let's come up with our signature poses!

00:00:35.130 --> 00:00:37.260
- I can't do something that uncool!
- Mari!

00:00:37.510 --> 00:00:40.560
- Since I'm "Red," little ol' me should be in the center.
- That's how it's gonna be!

00:00:41.560 --> 00:00:42.470
Okay!

00:00:42.470 --> 00:00:45.690
Then it's settled! RGB it is!

00:00:46.230 --> 00:00:50.520
Really. I just can't win against Asumi.

00:02:22.700 --> 00:02:25.330
What a disaster it was the other day, Sakuragi.

00:02:22.700 --> 00:02:25.330
MAY 10, 2021

00:02:25.450 --> 00:02:29.370
I really can't believe it.
I still get shivers when I hear about it.

00:02:29.370 --> 00:02:31.170
How did the hearing with SARG go?

00:02:32.880 --> 00:02:35.750
Well, I never want to go through it again.

00:02:35.880 --> 00:02:40.890
So, you chased your dog that kept
running away, and ended up there, huh?

00:02:41.680 --> 00:02:42.890
Yes.

00:02:43.050 --> 00:02:44.890
You know this guy, right?

00:02:45.430 --> 00:02:47.520
Th-That's someone I don't know.

00:02:47.810 --> 00:02:48.930
I see.

00:02:48.930 --> 00:02:55.150
Do you know how much you pay for compensation
when you stop a running train?

00:02:55.570 --> 00:02:59.030
Thanks to Koki's mediation,
everything ended without getting too serious.

00:02:59.030 --> 00:03:02.410
But it was really scary for various reasons!

00:03:04.530 --> 00:03:08.160
By the way,
have the RGB guys shown up here since?

00:03:08.160 --> 00:03:14.790
ITADAKI

00:03:08.160 --> 00:03:14.790
AOI BAKERY

00:03:08.540 --> 00:03:11.460
No, they haven't come by.
Do you need to talk to them?

00:03:11.460 --> 00:03:14.790
Yeah. It seems like they got into
another argument.

00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:17.840
So I thought I should at least
learn the details about it.

00:03:17.840 --> 00:03:19.920
Should I go see how they're doing?

00:03:19.920 --> 00:03:23.680
That'd be a big help.
Since we're so close to GourFes, I'm a bit busy.

00:03:23.680 --> 00:03:26.260
There's something I want to consult as well.

00:03:26.260 --> 00:03:29.770
Mari! Are you gonna be okay at GourFes
being so laid back like that?

00:03:29.980 --> 00:03:32.770
Yeah! We need Itadaki to win
its second year in a row

00:03:32.770 --> 00:03:36.020
at the 24th Ward Gourmet Festival
competitions at any cost.

00:03:36.270 --> 00:03:38.610
Huh? Well, we'll see about that.

00:03:38.610 --> 00:03:40.030
Put some more spirit into it!

00:03:40.240 --> 00:03:44.450
The Grand Prix winner this year is guaranteed
a collaboration with a major convenience store.

00:03:44.450 --> 00:03:45.700
Isn't that right, Sir?

00:03:45.870 --> 00:03:47.200
Yes, that's correct.

00:03:47.200 --> 00:03:51.330
You're part of the executive committee, right?
Come on, make Itadaki win!

00:03:51.460 --> 00:03:52.460
I can't.

00:03:52.460 --> 00:03:55.460
- You're so stubborn.
- I can't do what I can't do!

00:03:52.460 --> 00:03:55.460
THIRD ANNUAL
GOURMET FESTIVAL 2021

00:03:55.710 --> 00:03:58.750
KODA-GEN,
the famous comedian, will be coming too.

00:03:58.960 --> 00:04:00.760
Can you get me his autograph?

00:04:00.760 --> 00:04:02.720
W-Well, I think I can do that much.

00:04:03.090 --> 00:04:07.260
The future of the Takara Shopping Street
is riding on your Mari-Special!

00:04:07.260 --> 00:04:10.020
A critical blow of resurrection!

00:04:10.140 --> 00:04:12.100
I-I know that!

00:04:12.100 --> 00:04:15.520
So is your rival Takara Mall after all?

00:04:15.520 --> 00:04:20.990
Yes. It's been six months since that was built,
and our business suffers more and more.

00:04:21.650 --> 00:04:25.570
How about monjayaki,
the new soul food of the 24th Ward?

00:04:25.570 --> 00:04:28.990
If you pay with C-Pay, you get 85% cash back!

00:04:29.120 --> 00:04:31.910
Furthermore, they opened
all the same shop types as us!

00:04:31.910 --> 00:04:34.250
They totally want to put us out of business.

00:04:34.370 --> 00:04:38.590
And they're even nasty enough to have a monjayaki
place compete against our okonomiyaki!

00:04:38.790 --> 00:04:43.800
The okonomiyaki in 24th Ward
has a different origin from inland Tokyo,

00:04:43.800 --> 00:04:46.300
so I see no point in competing.

00:04:48.680 --> 00:04:53.640
However, ordinary people
have a different image.

00:04:54.350 --> 00:04:59.860
Hello. Yes, of course, everything is going well.

00:04:59.860 --> 00:05:02.860
I will give the details in the weekly report.

00:05:02.860 --> 00:05:04.700
I'm aware of that.

00:05:05.110 --> 00:05:08.570
We will keep it legal, with no violence.

00:05:08.950 --> 00:05:13.580
We'll meet all the conditions
so please use us for the construction.

00:05:13.580 --> 00:05:16.080
AOI BAKERY

00:05:14.410 --> 00:05:17.040
MAY 11, 2021

00:05:16.080 --> 00:05:19.880
<i>Originally from 24th Ward, the global artist 0th
is a recent topic of conversation</i>

00:05:19.880 --> 00:05:24.800
<i>as his graffiti satirizing the human rights movement
was found in Washington D.C.</i>

00:05:25.010 --> 00:05:28.930
<i>I found this in the morning.
The moment I saw it, I knew it was 0th.</i>

00:05:29.180 --> 00:05:31.970
His identity has been a mystery all this time.

00:05:31.970 --> 00:05:34.270
Yeah, 0th's art resonates with your heart.

00:05:34.270 --> 00:05:35.430
<i>On to the next topic.</i>

00:05:35.430 --> 00:05:38.810
A GIRL CHASED HER DOG ONTO THE TRACKS...
WHY COULDN'T THE KIZUNA TRAIN BE CONTROLLED REMOTELY?

00:05:35.890 --> 00:05:40.230
<i>People are raising doubts to the autonomous driving
of the Rainbow Line Express Kizuna Train.</i>

00:05:40.230 --> 00:05:45.190
They're doing this story again.
It was a really good thing that Mari was safe.

00:05:45.490 --> 00:05:48.700
Hey, Shu, help me out!

00:05:51.580 --> 00:05:55.450
I need menu ideas
for the GourFes this weekend.

00:05:56.120 --> 00:05:57.540
Ow...

00:05:57.540 --> 00:05:59.880
Sheesh! Listen to me.

00:06:00.170 --> 00:06:01.920
What? You have muscle cramps?

00:06:01.920 --> 00:06:06.340
Yeah. My body's been feeling really heavy
ever since that thing two days ago.

00:06:06.470 --> 00:06:09.550
Shu, you have monstrous athletic skills
to begin with,

00:06:09.550 --> 00:06:12.930
but that time, you really looked like
a hero from American comics.

00:06:13.810 --> 00:06:15.560
What are you talking about?

00:06:15.640 --> 00:06:20.650
The thing is, I got a phone call from Asumi.

00:06:20.940 --> 00:06:24.020
After that phone call,
I don't know why but I could really move.

00:06:24.320 --> 00:06:27.150
What are you talking about?
A phone call from Asumi?

00:06:27.150 --> 00:06:29.740
I really don't get it at all, either.

00:06:29.740 --> 00:06:34.410
But that was, without a doubt,
her voice. I think.

00:06:34.410 --> 00:06:36.500
Do you understand what you're saying?

00:06:36.500 --> 00:06:38.580
You're saying you got a call from a dead person!

00:06:38.580 --> 00:06:40.040
I know that!

00:06:40.540 --> 00:06:45.420
But when I picked up that phone call,
a scene started playing in my head.

00:06:45.880 --> 00:06:48.920
An scene of you being run over
by the Kizuna Train.

00:06:50.260 --> 00:06:54.050
Don't tell this to anyone.
I really don't understand it.

00:06:54.050 --> 00:06:56.310
Y-You don't have to tell me.

00:06:56.680 --> 00:07:01.270
Oh, but that means
I was rescued thanks to all of that.

00:07:02.690 --> 00:07:05.690
So, did you call Asumi back?

00:07:05.690 --> 00:07:07.650
Yeah. Many times.

00:07:08.360 --> 00:07:10.610
But I get voicemail every time.

00:07:13.370 --> 00:07:14.530
How to put it...

00:07:14.530 --> 00:07:17.410
I'm not really understanding how I'm feeling.

00:07:18.250 --> 00:07:19.620
Me, neither.

00:07:19.620 --> 00:07:21.460
But I can't help but think about it.

00:07:22.830 --> 00:07:25.880
It feels like this is no time
to be creating a new menu item.

00:07:26.550 --> 00:07:27.710
That's right.

00:07:27.710 --> 00:07:30.300
You have to mend fences
with both Ran and Koki.

00:07:30.670 --> 00:07:34.550
And I think that was simply a prank call.
Bye.

00:07:34.550 --> 00:07:37.810
Wh-Why do you know about our argument?

00:07:39.270 --> 00:07:43.230
When it comes to Asumi,
you really stop thinking about everything else.

00:07:44.560 --> 00:07:47.230
Asumi is no longer with us.

00:07:48.190 --> 00:07:50.150
What, even you, Mari?

00:07:50.530 --> 00:07:54.110
If Asumi is still alive,
it's something to be genuinely happy about.

00:07:56.160 --> 00:07:58.830
JULY 18, 2019

00:08:02.410 --> 00:08:03.790
Where to on our way home?

00:08:03.790 --> 00:08:05.130
Itadaki should do.

00:08:06.540 --> 00:08:11.130
Mari has team practice today,
so there's no Mari-Special.

00:08:11.420 --> 00:08:13.010
What a shame.

00:08:13.010 --> 00:08:14.970
Help me, Mr.24!

00:08:15.180 --> 00:08:17.560
I need the powers of a hero!

00:08:21.560 --> 00:08:23.350
Nice, goalkeeper!

00:08:23.480 --> 00:08:26.730
Hey, Asumi, is this a hero's job?

00:08:26.980 --> 00:08:28.520
But you still do it.

00:08:29.400 --> 00:08:32.280
I mean, you can't have a game
without a goalkeeper.

00:08:34.990 --> 00:08:35.910
Whoa.

00:08:38.120 --> 00:08:40.740
I knew I could count on Mr.24!

00:08:41.830 --> 00:08:43.290
You guys are cheating!

00:08:43.290 --> 00:08:46.170
What are you doing? Come on, let's go!

00:08:46.170 --> 00:08:47.250
Okay!

00:08:50.340 --> 00:08:51.460
Asumi?

00:08:51.460 --> 00:08:55.550
Yup. Asumin is my motif.
How is it? Does it look like her?

00:08:55.800 --> 00:08:59.930
Yeah, it looks like her.
But she looks kinda mature?

00:08:59.930 --> 00:09:01.930
That's how I drew her.

00:09:01.930 --> 00:09:03.480
I see.

00:09:05.140 --> 00:09:08.650
A souvenir. Bread crusts from Aoi Bakery.

00:09:11.360 --> 00:09:13.030
Since you're here, why don't you come in?

00:09:15.280 --> 00:09:17.280
Excuse me.

00:09:17.450 --> 00:09:20.030
Oh, Mari! Welcome!

00:09:20.200 --> 00:09:24.330
Kinako, it's been a while!
This is a pretty amazing place.

00:09:24.330 --> 00:09:27.120
Is this your first time in the DoRed hideout?

00:09:27.120 --> 00:09:29.630
Yeah. It really feels like a secret hideout.

00:09:29.880 --> 00:09:32.380
The SARG got their eyes on us.

00:09:32.670 --> 00:09:35.510
All our members are anonymous,
and never show their faces.

00:09:35.800 --> 00:09:39.050
Well, all my buddies in Shantytown
are on our side.

00:09:39.050 --> 00:09:41.640
So they shouldn't find out
who we really are that easily.

00:09:42.850 --> 00:09:44.770
Were you okay the other day?

00:09:44.770 --> 00:09:47.270
SARG totally reprimanded you
afterwards, right?

00:09:47.390 --> 00:09:52.780
Yeah. Like, who saved me,
and what my relationship to DoRed was.

00:09:52.980 --> 00:09:55.360
You didn't talk about Shu?

00:09:55.530 --> 00:09:57.950
I didn't. I'm not allowed to talk about him.

00:09:57.950 --> 00:10:00.950
But really, I'm glad that you were all right.

00:10:00.950 --> 00:10:04.160
<i>But what the hell was that vision?</i>

00:10:04.500 --> 00:10:08.250
<i>It looked like Asumin,
and it told me to pick one or the other.</i>

00:10:08.620 --> 00:10:11.420
<i>Does that mean we've changed the future?</i>

00:10:11.670 --> 00:10:12.670
Ran?

00:10:13.500 --> 00:10:15.510
Oh, sorry, it's nothing.

00:10:15.670 --> 00:10:18.300
Ran, your face looks kinda erotic.

00:10:18.300 --> 00:10:19.180
Don't joke.

00:10:19.590 --> 00:10:23.220
Oh! Ran, it's almost time!

00:10:23.220 --> 00:10:24.640
Huh? Time?

00:10:24.850 --> 00:10:27.350
The live painting stream!

00:10:27.810 --> 00:10:29.730
There are 30,000 people already waiting.

00:10:30.020 --> 00:10:33.440
Oh. Th-Then, good luck with your stream.

00:10:35.190 --> 00:10:36.610
See you later!

00:10:39.910 --> 00:10:41.450
Okay, Kinako.

00:10:41.780 --> 00:10:43.120
I'm starting it up!

00:10:43.580 --> 00:10:44.740
Okay!

00:10:45.540 --> 00:10:48.210
JULY 6, 2018

00:10:46.750 --> 00:10:50.620
I don't think little ol' me
is really suited for stuff like this.

00:10:50.880 --> 00:10:52.750
You say that,
but you look like you're having fun.

00:10:52.750 --> 00:10:54.420
Yeah, you're totally on a roll.

00:10:54.420 --> 00:10:58.090
Oh no, art is where you express your attitude,

00:10:58.090 --> 00:11:02.090
so even if you draw on a legal wall,
it's not bomb and evil.

00:11:02.300 --> 00:11:03.800
That's not true!

00:11:04.050 --> 00:11:08.890
Ran, your art echoes with people's hearts
regardless of it being legal or illegal.

00:11:08.890 --> 00:11:11.190
More people should get to look at it!

00:11:12.100 --> 00:11:14.730
Those words echo even more.

00:11:15.440 --> 00:11:16.980
There, I'm done!

00:11:17.400 --> 00:11:20.650
U-Um, can I take a picture?

00:11:21.360 --> 00:11:23.700
Of course. You can take as much as you want.

00:11:23.870 --> 00:11:25.660
Thank you so much.

00:11:25.910 --> 00:11:29.040
Um, if you don't mind, can I take a video too?

00:11:29.040 --> 00:11:29.870
A video?

00:11:30.080 --> 00:11:32.790
Live painting! How wonderful!

00:11:32.960 --> 00:11:35.630
Sounds good! That's perfect!

00:11:37.630 --> 00:11:39.590
CAFÉ SHIROTSUMEGUSA

00:11:42.840 --> 00:11:44.090
Sakuragi.

00:11:44.090 --> 00:11:46.430
Hey there.
Working on an assignment for college?

00:11:47.310 --> 00:11:51.730
Oh, sorry. I only allow emergency notifications
while I'm studying.

00:11:51.730 --> 00:11:53.560
I'm surprised you found me here.

00:11:53.560 --> 00:11:56.190
I called the Suido house,
and Ms. Tsuzuragawa...

00:11:57.650 --> 00:12:00.280
So what's up? Something urgent?

00:12:00.530 --> 00:12:03.110
You had an argument with Shu
two days ago, didn't you?

00:12:03.110 --> 00:12:05.280
Mr. Shirakaba was worried.

00:12:05.280 --> 00:12:07.790
- What, you came here to mediate?
- Welcome.

00:12:08.040 --> 00:12:09.250
Have you decided what to order?

00:12:09.250 --> 00:12:10.830
Oh, one blend coffee, please.

00:12:11.080 --> 00:12:13.790
One blend. Will that be all?

00:12:13.790 --> 00:12:14.790
Yes.

00:12:14.790 --> 00:12:17.710
All right. I'll be right back.

00:12:17.710 --> 00:12:21.590
Well, that's just an incidental
that I'm curious about, but...

00:12:21.840 --> 00:12:23.130
For now...

00:12:24.470 --> 00:12:27.180
Hey Koki, you know about Mon Jungle?

00:12:28.430 --> 00:12:30.600
The flagship restaurant in Takara Mall?

00:12:30.600 --> 00:12:34.900
Yeah. Apparently my store and theirs
are favored to win this year's GourFes.

00:12:35.060 --> 00:12:37.980
Everyone on the shopping street
is getting hyped up for it.

00:12:35.350 --> 00:12:38.770
<i>GourFes. It's already
that time of the year, huh?</i>

00:12:40.610 --> 00:12:42.900
It's the 24th Ward Gourmet Festival!

00:12:40.610 --> 00:12:43.570
DECEMBER 14, 2018

00:12:43.240 --> 00:12:45.660
It's the 24th Ward Gourmet Festival!

00:12:45.780 --> 00:12:47.030
Please come take a look!

00:12:47.240 --> 00:12:49.990
GOURMET FESTIVAL

00:12:47.780 --> 00:12:49.990
It's the 24th Ward Gourmet Festival.

00:12:49.990 --> 00:12:52.750
SUMIRE PHARMACY

00:12:53.160 --> 00:12:56.000
Not many people are taking these.

00:12:56.000 --> 00:12:58.460
- I promised Father that I would make it a success.
- Brother!

00:12:58.750 --> 00:13:01.840
Asumi. You were in charge
of the Nihama Station area, right?

00:13:01.840 --> 00:13:03.920
I'm done passing them out.

00:13:04.180 --> 00:13:08.430
Come on, nobody would accept flyers
if you look like that.

00:13:08.430 --> 00:13:09.510
Smile. Smile!

00:13:09.850 --> 00:13:11.470
L-Like this?

00:13:11.720 --> 00:13:14.810
Maybe a bit different.

00:13:14.810 --> 00:13:17.610
Koki, you're so secretive. You should've told us.

00:13:17.610 --> 00:13:18.730
Sakuragi.

00:13:18.730 --> 00:13:21.860
That's right. Let's make GourFes a success!

00:13:20.270 --> 00:13:22.900
This is a good opportunity
to showcase our croquettes!

00:13:21.860 --> 00:13:23.860
Is this all the flyers to pass out?

00:13:24.070 --> 00:13:26.570
Yes, for today at least.

00:13:27.700 --> 00:13:30.450
Asumi, did you call everyone?

00:13:30.950 --> 00:13:34.080
Well, yeah. Come on,
we should pass them out, too.

00:13:34.080 --> 00:13:35.460
Y-Yeah.

00:13:37.040 --> 00:13:38.540
Thank you so much!

00:13:40.130 --> 00:13:42.380
Oh, that was a good smile!

00:13:45.550 --> 00:13:50.140
I really learned a lot by being part of operations
as a member of the executive committee.

00:13:51.390 --> 00:13:56.640
<i>That's right. Koki is the founder, so he can't really
side with anyone in particular.</i>

00:13:57.600 --> 00:13:59.360
Are you worried about something?

00:13:59.360 --> 00:14:04.780
No, it's nothing. I was thinking about
how GourFes will be hyped up again this year.

00:14:07.110 --> 00:14:09.700
Mr. Koki, thank you for waiting.

00:14:10.620 --> 00:14:12.160
Sorry to trouble you.

00:14:12.280 --> 00:14:14.160
No, don't worry about it.

00:14:14.160 --> 00:14:17.460
- But I thought I told you not to hide transmi—
- About that phone call...

00:14:18.000 --> 00:14:22.880
We haven't determined the culprit, but someone
seems to be spoofing Miss Asumi's number.

00:14:23.800 --> 00:14:25.840
We will continue the investigation.

00:14:25.920 --> 00:14:27.800
I see. I'm counting on you.

00:14:28.380 --> 00:14:30.680
<i>That phone call, and the future prognostication.</i>

00:14:30.890 --> 00:14:33.390
<i>And that power coursing through my body.</i>

00:14:33.680 --> 00:14:38.980
<i>The scoundrel pretending to be Asumi
holds the key to unraveling all the secrets.</i>

00:14:42.400 --> 00:14:45.900
24TH WARD GOURMET FESTIVAL

00:14:43.400 --> 00:14:45.900
GourFes is this weekend, huh?

00:14:46.190 --> 00:14:47.820
I don't have any time.

00:14:49.280 --> 00:14:49.780
Huh?

00:14:50.280 --> 00:14:53.410
Mr. Shirakaba and Mr. Chikushi from SARG?

00:14:55.330 --> 00:14:58.750
What did you want to ask me, Mr. Shirakaba?

00:14:59.040 --> 00:15:03.170
What is Takara Mall... rather,
what is Yabusame, after?

00:15:03.540 --> 00:15:06.380
So you were aware of Yabusame?

00:15:06.380 --> 00:15:10.130
It was a quasi-gang organization, right?
Someone I used to know is a part of it.

00:15:10.680 --> 00:15:15.430
Then this will be quick.
Well, it's basically what you're thinking.

00:15:11.430 --> 00:15:14.850
<i>Why am I doing something
like eavesdropping?</i>

00:15:16.100 --> 00:15:21.650
Takara Mall is operated by Yabusame
through a paper company.

00:15:21.650 --> 00:15:25.770
What is Yabusame after by using GourFes?

00:15:25.770 --> 00:15:28.400
Isn't it a bit too much money
to be moving around?

00:15:28.650 --> 00:15:32.450
For the past few years, they've been making money
by being borderline-illegal land sharks

00:15:32.450 --> 00:15:35.160
so they can be given construction contracts.

00:15:35.410 --> 00:15:38.000
Their objective is to buy up
the entire Takara Shopping Street?

00:15:38.000 --> 00:15:43.500
Mon Jungle, operated by Yabusame,
will do whatever it takes in order to win.

00:15:43.500 --> 00:15:46.880
Takara Mall is supposed to be
under Suido Zaibatsu's wing. It can't be—

00:15:46.880 --> 00:15:49.920
Whoa. I can't officially make
any further comments.

00:15:49.920 --> 00:15:51.590
So I'll be seeing you later.

00:15:53.840 --> 00:15:55.350
What’s going on?

00:15:56.180 --> 00:15:57.430
Sakuragi.

00:15:57.810 --> 00:15:59.310
You were listening?

00:16:01.640 --> 00:16:06.610
That kinda sounded like
the winner has already been decided.

00:16:06.610 --> 00:16:09.240
- Sakuragi, you really are smart.
- Mr. Shirakaba!

00:16:09.240 --> 00:16:10.190
It's all right!

00:16:10.190 --> 00:16:13.700
I won't allow any dishonesty. Trust me!

00:16:15.320 --> 00:16:17.910
All right, I will believe you.

00:16:18.120 --> 00:16:21.620
But you're always doing things
for other people, huh?

00:16:21.790 --> 00:16:25.210
Even though you're no longer our teacher,
you take care of us.

00:16:25.210 --> 00:16:30.550
It's my personality, or rather, my own beliefs.

00:16:29.170 --> 00:16:31.720
SEPTEMBER 20, 2019

00:16:30.880 --> 00:16:35.590
After school, you guys are hanging out
at Takara Elementary that's been abandoned, aren't you?

00:16:35.590 --> 00:16:38.760
They're demolishing it for redevelopment,
so don't go there anymore.

00:16:38.970 --> 00:16:40.600
- We know that!
- Of course we don't want that!

00:16:40.600 --> 00:16:44.560
It's a school that has history in the 24th Ward,
and you're going to demolish it?

00:16:44.650 --> 00:16:46.730
- It's our alma mater filled with memories!
- Sheesh, so noisy.

00:16:46.730 --> 00:16:48.650
That building can still be used!

00:16:48.650 --> 00:16:51.570
The school closed from low birth rates,
so that has nothing to do with it.

00:16:51.570 --> 00:16:54.030
At least you can reuse it for something else.

00:16:54.030 --> 00:16:57.410
What are you gonna do if you get hurt
in a place that's off limits?

00:16:57.700 --> 00:16:59.290
Don't be throwing tantrums!

00:16:59.660 --> 00:17:04.160
And so, let's start the meeting
for the conservation of Takara Elementary!

00:17:04.540 --> 00:17:06.250
Okay everyone, speak your opinions!

00:17:07.460 --> 00:17:10.500
The fact that it's a school
with our memories is huge,

00:17:10.500 --> 00:17:13.300
but it's still serving
as a place where boys and girls relax, right?

00:17:13.300 --> 00:17:15.930
And there was that historical bit.

00:17:15.930 --> 00:17:18.720
Yeah. Takara Elementary was the first school

00:17:18.720 --> 00:17:23.560
that was built on this land after the war,
as the history of being an outside territory had begun.

00:17:23.770 --> 00:17:26.770
And a spot that I have memories
with my mother.

00:17:26.940 --> 00:17:28.730
Mrs. Kanae, huh?

00:17:28.860 --> 00:17:33.490
That's right, we can't let
the school be destroyed for her sake, too.

00:17:33.490 --> 00:17:35.030
Okay, thanks for waiting.

00:17:35.530 --> 00:17:37.950
Today's Mari-Special is a "blackboard"!

00:17:37.950 --> 00:17:39.530
Enjoy drawing to your heart's content!

00:17:40.030 --> 00:17:41.990
This leave quite a visual impact.

00:17:41.990 --> 00:17:43.620
Isn't this a bit too black?

00:17:43.620 --> 00:17:46.420
It's fine. I'll start drawing!

00:17:46.420 --> 00:17:47.580
This is it!

00:17:47.750 --> 00:17:50.710
Mari, this is it! What a nice idea!

00:17:51.130 --> 00:17:54.220
Let's cover Takara Elementary with graffiti!

00:18:06.350 --> 00:18:07.850
Let's spread the word.

00:18:08.100 --> 00:18:09.360
There.

00:18:19.820 --> 00:18:24.040
TURNING AN ALMA MATER INTO AN ART SANCTUARY!

00:18:20.070 --> 00:18:24.040
This movement has meaning
in preserving a historical building,

00:18:24.660 --> 00:18:27.540
<i>and deepening the bonds
of the community in this area.</i>

00:18:28.670 --> 00:18:30.290
How is it?

00:18:30.670 --> 00:18:34.170
If RGB all gather up, nothing is impossible!

00:18:37.800 --> 00:18:44.180
STUDENTS HANGING OUT AT AN ABANDONED SCHOOL
THAT HAD PLANS FOR BEING DEMOLISHED

00:18:38.180 --> 00:18:44.180
Mr. Shirakaba, regarding our students creating
a movement to overthrow the government's decision.

00:18:44.180 --> 00:18:45.930
Were you aware of this?

00:18:45.930 --> 00:18:50.100
It's been reported on TV, and we've been
getting heavy pressure from the PTA.

00:18:50.100 --> 00:18:51.860
So, Mr. Shirakaba?

00:18:51.860 --> 00:18:54.730
Those are students
in your homeroom class, correct?

00:18:55.190 --> 00:19:00.110
Two months ago, I directly advised them
to leave the abandoned school.

00:19:00.110 --> 00:19:03.330
However, I regret doing that now.

00:19:03.450 --> 00:19:06.540
They've taught us that the abandoned school

00:19:06.540 --> 00:19:10.960
surpasses the conveniences of adults,
and is an important place for the 24th Ward.

00:19:11.710 --> 00:19:16.130
Chairman, can you make it work in a way
so that the government can acknowledge

00:19:16.130 --> 00:19:19.380
that said location
is worth preserving culturally?

00:19:21.140 --> 00:19:25.890
I am thankful
that you buy so much into my children.

00:19:26.180 --> 00:19:30.390
However, considering my position,
I must present several conditions.

00:19:31.400 --> 00:19:33.650
You can't!
You have to wait for Shu and the others.

00:19:33.650 --> 00:19:34.940
I just called them!

00:19:34.940 --> 00:19:37.900
But if I don't go in right now,
we can't save everyone.

00:19:39.320 --> 00:19:40.150
I-I'll go—

00:19:40.150 --> 00:19:41.200
Mari!

00:19:42.780 --> 00:19:46.830
All right. The firefighters will be here,
so let's go and guide them.

00:19:46.990 --> 00:19:48.950
We have to have the onlookers move, too.

00:19:48.950 --> 00:19:49.910
Oh, right.

00:19:49.910 --> 00:19:51.210
Mari, hurry!

00:19:51.210 --> 00:19:52.170
Okay!

00:19:57.590 --> 00:19:58.340
Asumi?

00:19:58.760 --> 00:20:00.090
- Asumi!
- I'm sorry!

00:20:00.260 --> 00:20:02.930
We can't save everyone
if we wait for the firefighters!

00:20:03.470 --> 00:20:05.890
You're gonna... die...

00:20:06.220 --> 00:20:07.260
You can't...

00:20:07.260 --> 00:20:09.060
Y-You're not Shu.

00:20:09.850 --> 00:20:11.560
You'll die.

00:20:15.690 --> 00:20:20.950
<i>I'm keeping this footage
for self-admonishment.</i>

00:20:21.490 --> 00:20:26.200
<i>Please don't forget what happened today, me.</i>

00:20:28.240 --> 00:20:31.120
We were always saying
it was for everyone's sake.

00:20:31.410 --> 00:20:35.290
We kept saying it, and kept acting.

00:20:35.880 --> 00:20:39.130
But you can't die for it.

00:20:52.810 --> 00:20:54.940
It's already been a year, huh?

00:20:55.770 --> 00:20:59.980
I'm no good. I keep striving to keep up
with someone younger than me.

00:21:00.280 --> 00:21:03.740
I can't make fun of Shu, huh?

00:21:05.070 --> 00:21:11.080
Asumi, I can't handle RGB all by myself.

00:21:16.920 --> 00:21:18.130
I'm home.

00:21:18.130 --> 00:21:20.210
Welcome back. You were out pretty late.

00:21:20.210 --> 00:21:22.210
- I was thinking a bit—
- You're late, Mari.

00:21:22.840 --> 00:21:25.220
We've started the tactical meeting without you.

00:21:25.220 --> 00:21:30.060
More like Mari, you asked Ran and Koki too?
I should already be more than enough.

00:21:30.260 --> 00:21:31.520
What are you talking about?

00:21:31.520 --> 00:21:34.850
Sakuragi was relying on me.
You guys are just afterthoughts.

00:21:34.850 --> 00:21:37.610
You think you can win against little ol' me
in coming up with ideas?

00:21:35.730 --> 00:21:37.610
Well Mari, take care of the rest for me.

00:21:37.860 --> 00:21:39.940
Good luck on making that menu item!

00:21:39.940 --> 00:21:41.190
Y-Yeah.

00:21:41.360 --> 00:21:42.860
Come on, Mari. Let's get started.

00:21:42.860 --> 00:21:45.070
We have to eat something first.

00:21:45.360 --> 00:21:49.830
Sheesh! This is why RGB are so...

00:21:50.280 --> 00:21:54.620
Okay, let's start the Mari-Special
Development Meeting for GourFes!

00:21:56.290 --> 00:21:57.290
I'm so full.

00:21:57.290 --> 00:21:59.340
All the blood
is going from my head to my stomach.

00:21:59.710 --> 00:22:02.090
We said we were just tasting,
but we ate too much.

00:22:05.880 --> 00:22:07.380
Asumi?

00:22:07.640 --> 00:22:08.930
It's thanks to you, Mari.

00:22:09.680 --> 00:22:13.390
Everyone can be so mischievous
because Itadaki is around.

00:22:13.390 --> 00:22:15.560
Even if they argue, or at odds with each other,

00:22:15.890 --> 00:22:18.400
there's always a place for them
to come back to.

00:22:18.400 --> 00:22:20.560
Is that so?

00:22:20.560 --> 00:22:23.820
Yes. It's all thanks to you, Mari.

00:22:25.820 --> 00:22:28.110
I hope that's the case.

00:22:30.530 --> 00:22:31.450
Hey, Mari.

00:22:31.700 --> 00:22:33.370
They said it'll be sunny for GourFes!

00:22:36.750 --> 00:22:38.540
All right, let's do this!

00:23:51.360 --> 00:23:53.620
What will the observation results be?

00:23:54.030 --> 00:23:57.160
I pray that it still hasn't converged.
